# TypeScript and React Style Guide

General

- Always define explicit prop types for components and type signatures for exported functions
- Do not use `any`; prefer precise types and generics
- Naming: use verbs for functions and meaningful nouns for variables

Components

- Use function components with explicit prop types: `type Props = { ... }`
- Keep internal UI state in the component and business state in Zustand stores
- Hooks: use `useEffect` for side effects and `useMemo` or `useCallback` for memoization

Data fetching

- Make API calls from services in [src/lib](mdc:src/lib) or from stores, not directly from page components
- Handle errors and loading states; display `LoadingSpinner` from [src/components/ui/LoadingSpinner.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/LoadingSpinner.tsx)

UI and styling

- Use Tailwind classes and Shadcn UI components from [src/components/ui](mdc:src/components/ui)
- Do not inline large style blocks; extract them into classes or utilities

Routing

- Use React Router v6 and configure routes in [src/routes/index.tsx](mdc:src/routes/index.tsx)

Testability and maintainability

- Avoid deep nesting and use early returns
- Extract utilities and repeated logic into separate functions or hooks
